ource":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Chase, Jefferson unanimous All-Pros; Lamar beats out Allen at QB","description":"Lamar Jackson beat out Josh Allen at quarterback, and Ja'Marr Chase and Justin Jefferson are unanimous choices for the Associated Press 2024 NFL All-Pro Team.","published":"2025-01-10T21:22:31.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/43359578/chase-jefferson-unanimous-all-pros-lamar-beats-allen-qb","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Detroit Lions fake punt on their own 20-yard line vs. Bucs","description":"The Detroit Lions pulled from their bag of tricks in the second quarter against the Tampa Bay Buccaneers.","published":"2024-09-15T18:54:50.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/41274395/detroit-lions-fake-punt-their-own-20-yard-line-vs-bucs","type":"Story","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Lions' Jack Fox signs extension, becomes highest-paid punter","description":"The Lions' Jack Fox, who leads the NFL in gross punting average since 2020, will become the league's highest-paid punter with his 3-year extension.","published":"2022-10-22T14:05:42.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/34852636/lions-jack-fox-signs-extension-becomes-highest-paid-punter","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Chiefs' 53-man roster projection leaves off RB Carlos Hyde","description":"We predict the Chiefs will only go with three running backs, which could be dangerous given none of them have been tested over a full season.","published":"2019-08-28T10:00:21.000+00:00","url":"http://espn.com/blog/kansas-city-chiefs/post/_/id/26584/chiefs-53-man-roster-projection-leaves-off-rb-carlos-hyde","type":"BlogEntry","byline":"Adam Teicher","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Chiefs' 53-man roster projection has deep running back group","description":"The Chiefs go into camp thin on the offensive line, but Hill's disciplinary issues hang over the start of Kansas City's season.","published":"2019-07-24T12:00:09.000+00:00","url":"http://espn.com/blog/kansas-city-chiefs/post/_/id/26500/chiefs-53-man-roster-projection-deep-running-back-group","type":"BlogEntry","byline":"Adam Teicher","source":"ESPN"}],"wiki":{"title":"Jack Fox (American football)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jack_Fox_(American_football)","description":"American football punter (born 1996)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:32:28Z","intro":"John Edward Fox (born September 1, 1996) is an American professional football punter for the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL). He played college football for the Rice Owls. Fox joined the Lions as a rookie in 2019, since earning two Pro Bowl and All-Pro selections; a first-team selection in 2024 and a second-team selection in 2020.\nHe is second in yards per punt in NFL history at (48.4) yards.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Fox was born in Dallas, Texas and grew up in St. Louis, Missouri. He attended Ladue Horton Watkins High School, where he played baseball and football. As a senior, he was named first-team All-State as a punter and to the second-team as a placekicker while also passing for 1,900 yards and 18 touchdowns at quarterback."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Fox was both a kicker and punter for four seasons at Rice University. As a freshman he handled kickoffs and made 12 of 12 extra point attempts and one of two field goal attempts. He became the Owls punter going into his sophomore year and was named honorable mention All-Conference USA (C-USA) after punting 75 times for 3,051 yards (40.7 average) with two extra points and one field goal made. As a junior, Fox had 56 punts for 2,480 yards (44.3 average) with one extra point attempted and made and was named second-team All-C-USA. He also became the primary kicker for Rice as a senior and was named first-team All-conference and the Conference Special Teams Player of the Year, as well as a finalist for the Ray Guy Award, after punting 80 times 3,636 yards (45.5 average) with 23 extra points attempted and making 5 of 12 field goal attempts."},{"key":"career","title":"Professional career","text":"KANSAS CITY CHIEFS\nFox was signed by the Kansas City Chiefs as an undrafted free agent on May 4, 2019. He was waived during final roster cuts. Fox was re-signed by the Chiefs to their practice squad on October 30, 2019, after the team's punter, Dustin Colquitt, suffered a quad strain but was released one week later on November 6.\n\nDETROIT LIONS\nFox was signed to the Detroit Lions practice squad on December 5, 2019, where he spent the rest of the season. He was signed to a futures contract at the end of the season. Fox was named the Lions opening day punter at the end of training camp, beating out Arryn Siposs. Fox made his NFL debut on September 13, 2020, in the season opener against the Chicago Bears, punting 4 times for 197 yards (49.3 average) with two punts inside the 20-yard line. Fox was named the National Football Conference (NFC) Special Teams Player of the Month for September.\nFox finished his first season with 59 punts for an average of 49.1 yards and a net average of 44.8, both Lions records, and was named to the 2021 Pro Bowl and second-team All-Pro. He was given an exclusive-rights free agent tender by the Lions on March 4, 2021. He signed the one-year contract on April 23.\nOn October 22, 2022, Fox signed a three-year, $11.325 million contract extension with the Lions, making him the highest-paid punter in the league. In the 2023 NFL season, Fox made it to the NFC Championship with the Lions where he punted twice for 108 yards (54.0 average). The Lions would ultimately lose to the San Francisco 49ers 31–34 after allowing a 17-point comeback.\nIn Week 3 of the 2024 season, Fox punted five times, with four inside the 20-yard line in a 20-13 win over the Arizona Cardinals, earning NFC Special Teams Player of the Week. Fox finished the season with 45 punts for 2,295 yards. He led the league in both yards per punt (51.0) and net yards per punt (45.8), earning Pro Bowl honors for his performance. In the 2025 season, he finished with 56 punts for 2,611 yards for a 46.6 average.\nIn Week 8 of the 2026 season against the until then undefeated [[2026 Minnesota Vikings season\n|Minnesota Vikings]], Fox punted four times, averaging 46.5 yards per boot and placing three punts inside the 20-yard line, earning him NFC Special Teams Player of the Week."},{"key":"personal","title":"Personal life","text":"In the 2021 off-season, Fox organized a young specialist camp where he invited youth kickers and punters from the Detroit area. An avid Yu-Gi-Oh! player, Fox showed his Instagram followers his collection of nearly 600 cards in a live stream in June of 2025.  In a 2024 interview with the Detroit Metro Times, Fox referenced his childhood interest in Harry Potter, describing himself as a \"Hufflepuff, perfectly at home here in Detroit\"."}],"wikidataId":"Q104834292","social":{}},"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3916370","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/F/FoxxJa01.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/jack-fox/34735","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/jack-fox/8227","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jack_Fox_(American_football)"},"insights":["Ranks 1st of 32 qualified punters in net average.","Ranks 6th of 32 qualified punters in inside-20 %.","On the field for 30% of Detroit’s special-teams snaps this season.","2026 cap number of $4.0M is the 16th-largest on the roster.","Contract expires after this season."]}